From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam Adrian <4.adam.adrian@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 12:50:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] input/misc/soc_button_array: fix boot-time race with
 pinctrl GPIO controller

On Surface devices using MSHW0040 (Pro 4 and later, Book 1/2, Laptop),
soc_button_array's probe() calls gpiod_count() to look up the button
GPIOs. If the platform's pinctrl driver (pinctrl_sunrisepoint on
Skylake-based Pro 4, pinctrl_icelake/pinctrl_tigerlake on later
generations) has not yet registered its gpiochip when udev coldplugs
MSHW0040, gpiod_count() returns -ENOENT and the driver bails out with
a hard -ENODEV. Because this is not -EPROBE_DEFER, the driver core
never retries once the pinctrl module finishes loading, and the
physical power/volume buttons stay dead until the module is manually
reloaded.

Ported from jonpetersathan/linux-cachyos-surface-patches (patches/6.18
and patches/6.12, 0009-surface-button.patch), which fixes the same
race for wake-from-suspend on Surface Laptop 5 / Surface Pro 9 (see
linux-surface/linux-surface issues #1910, #1805, #1392, #1481).
Adjusted here to also softdep on pinctrl_sunrisepoint for Skylake-era
Pro 4 hardware.

Patchset: surface-button-local
---
 drivers/input/misc/soc_button_array.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/input/misc/soc_button_array.c b/drivers/input/misc/soc_button_array.c
index 43b5d56383e3..8f2a1c7e0000 100644
--- a/drivers/input/misc/soc_button_array.c
+++ b/drivers/input/misc/soc_button_array.c
@@ -454,8 +454,9 @@ static int soc_button_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)

 	error = gpiod_count(dev, NULL);
 	if (error < 0) {
-		dev_dbg(dev, "no GPIO attached, ignoring...\n");
-		return -ENODEV;
+		if (error == -ENOENT)
+			return -EPROBE_DEFER;
+		return error;
 	}

 	priv = devm_kzalloc(dev, sizeof(*priv), GFP_KERNEL);
@@ -604,3 +605,4 @@ module_platform_driver(soc_button_driver);

 MODULE_DESCRIPTION("Windows-compatible SoC Button Array driver");
 MODULE_LICENSE("GPL");
+MODULE_SOFTDEP("pre: pinctrl_sunrisepoint pinctrl_icelake pinctrl_tigerlake");
--
2.52.0
